screens.prose:
A **template** writes the function once, with the type as a parameter `T`. Each call fixes `T` from its argument.

```cpp
template <typename T>
T max_of(const std::vector<T>& xs) {
    T best = xs[0];
    for (const T& x : xs) if (best < x) best = x;
    return best;
}

max_of(std::vector<int>{3, 9, 4});
max_of(std::vector<double>{101.5, 99.8});
max_of(std::vector<int>{7, 2});
max_of(std::vector<std::string>{"BARC", "AZN"});
```

